<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ion Iliescu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1930–2025</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ion Iliescu was a Romanian politician who led the National Salvation Front after the revolution of December 1989 overthrew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicolae-ceausescu">Nicolae Ceaușescu</a>. A former communist official, he was elected president in 1990 and again in 1992 and 2000. His first years in power were marked by the violent miners' interventions in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bucharest">Bucharest</a>, while his later term saw <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a> prepare to join <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nato">NATO</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-union">European Union</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ion-iliescu.jpg" alt="Ion Iliescu" width="320" height="465" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Aluísio/Vice-presidência da República · CC BY 3.0 br · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ion_Iliescu_(2004).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
